INT. CATHEDRAL BELL TOWER OBSERVATION POST - DAY

A cramped stone chamber beneath the bells. Narrow arrow-slit windows. Sandbags stacked against the wall. A field telephone on a plank, a pair of binoculars on a nail.

CAPTAIN HENRY ABERNETHY-LOWE stands at the east slit, field glasses at his eyes. He is tall, spare, and impeccable, his uniform pressed even in the dust. CORPORAL TOMMASO RICCI sits on an ammunition crate, a rifle across his knees, cleaning it with a rag. PRIVATE ELIJAH STONE-BARNES, barely nineteen, huddles by the stairwell door, a mug of tea cold in his hands.

The captain lowers the glasses. He does not turn.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Anything?

RICCI
Nothing, sir.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Then keep looking.

Ricci nods, not looking up. The private watches the captain, who watches the horizon. A great quiet fills the tower.

RADIO OPERATOR (V.O.)
(field phone, crackling)
Eagle's Nest, this is Baker Two. Report.

Abernethy-Lowe crosses the floor, lifts the receiver, and holds it with two fingers.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Baker Two, Eagle's Nest. Position quiet. No movement.

RADIO OPERATOR (V.O.)
(field phone)
Understood. Command wants a sweep of the north road at sixteen hundred.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Acknowledged.

He hangs up. Stands very still, his hand lingering on the receiver. Elijah sets down the mug.

ELIJAH
Sir?

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Private.

ELIJAH
Is it true what they say about the bells?

ABERNETHY-LOWE
What do they say?

ELIJAH
That they ring on their own before an attack.

Ricci snorts, rubbing the rifle. The captain turns, finally, and studies the boy.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
They ring when the wind is wrong. That's all.

ELIJAH
Then why do you keep checking?

The captain does not answer. A long pause. High above, in the dark of the belfry, a single bell hums, a faint, shivering note, not a ring, not yet.

Ricci puts down the rifle. Abernethy-Lowe lifts his glasses. Elijah stands. They all look at the arrow-slit, where the afternoon light has gone a strange, pale gold.

RICCI
(softly)
Wind.

ABERNETHY-LOWE
Wind.

The bell hums again. This time, it rings.
